cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use roottrait, please cite it as below."
title: "roottrait: root traits from binary masks and calibrated mask degradations for testing segmentation metrics"
abstract: >-
  Root segmentation models are compared by Dice overlap, but their masks are used to measure root
  traits. roottrait computes twelve root traits from binary masks, grouped by how a local pixel
  error enters them, and provides six named segmentation failures whose severity is calibrated per
  mask to an exact Dice loss, so that different failures can be compared at the same overlap. It
  also decomposes a prediction's errors into four kinds and fills small annotation holes that
  otherwise inflate skeleton junction counts. The repository reproduces every result in the
  accompanying manuscript, including experiments on the PRMI minirhizotron dataset.
type: software
